<title>USA: General Electric employees ratify contract.</title>
<headline>General Electric employees ratify contract.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFIELD, Connecticut 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of two unions representing 27,000 General Electric Co employees have ratified new three-year contracts with the company, a news release issued Wednesday by General Electric said.</p>
<p>Union officials informed General Electric that voting by local memberships of the International Union of Electronic Workers and United Electrical Workers was completed today.</p>
<p>Ratification completes the unions' approval process for the contract agreements that were reached June 29 between General Electric and union negotiators, the news release said.</p>
<p>Contract terms were not given in the release.</p>
</text>
